    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d39">

                <pb facs="0049" n="35" sameAs="frus:frus1947v06/pg35"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.45C21/7–347: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consulate General at
                        Rangoon</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-07-07T17:00:00-04:00">July 7, 1947—5
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>252. Urtel 550, July 3.<anchor n="86" xml:id="d39-f1"/> Revised draft consular
                    convention sent with</p>
                <p>Vice Consul Thurgood<anchor n="87" xml:id="d39-f2"/> may be presented GOB unless
                    you believe presentation now would delay receipt satisfactory reply your letter
                    June 5 to Aung San on subject extent consular jurisdiction.<anchor n="88"
                        xml:id="d39-f3"/>
                </p>
                <p>Re your last para Dept expects GOB suggest date. (See final sentence Dept reply
                    Brit Emb Deptel 211 June 6) Dept considers that <list>
                        <label>1.</label>
                        <item>Brit note June 2<anchor n="86" xml:id="d39-f4"/>
                        </item>
                        <label>2.</label>
                        <item>Dept reply June 6</item>
                        <label>3.</label>
                        <item>Brit answer to questions asked by Dept and Brit request for agreement
                            on So Nyun</item>
                        <label>4.</label>
                        <item> Dept reply through Brit Emb</item>
                        <label/>
                        <item>will constitute “notes establishing diplomatic relations”. Only
                            additional prerequisite public announcement is receipt by you of
                            satisfactory answer your June 5 letter. </item>
                    </list>
                </p>
                <p>Your proposed title: “Chargé d’Affaires ad interim of the United States of
                    America.”</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Marshall</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d39-f1" n="86" xml:id="d39-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d39-f2" n="87" xml:id="d39-f2-content">
                <p>Harriet C. Thurgood, Vice Consul at Colombo, on June 6 was appointed temporarily
                    as Vice Consul at Rangoon.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d39-f3" n="88" xml:id="d39-f3-content">
                <p>See telegram 486, June 14, from Rangoon, <ref target="#pg32">p. 32</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d39-f4" n="86" xml:id="d39-f4-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
